-- Version 38 → 39: a status can say that its issues no longer block anything.
--
-- One new `statuses` column, `unblocks`. Its reasoning — why a flag rather than a
-- column name, and why a closing column unblocks without it — lives beside it in
-- Statuses.sq and is not repeated here.
--
-- Plain ALTER TABLE: single-column, NOT NULL with a constant default, the case
-- 36.sqm describes.
--
-- ── Nothing to back-fill ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
--
-- 0 on every existing column is the behaviour every board had before this ran: a
-- blocker stops blocking only once it is closed. Arming the flag on, say, "Ready for
-- test" un-greys cards on everybody's board, so it is left for an admin to do
-- deliberately rather than guessed at from column names here.

ALTER TABLE statuses ADD COLUMN unblocks INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;
